  "body": "## What was broken\n\nThe deferred install path (Windows, when the app is already running) stages a verified wheel and spawns a detached helper to finish the install after the launchers exit. The helper invoked uv by placing a **command string** at statement position:\n\n```powershell\n$argumentsLiteral 2>&1 | Out-String | Out-Null\n```\n\n`$argumentsLiteral` was the string `` & 'C:\\...\\uv.exe' @('tool','install',...) ``. In PowerShell a statement-position string is treated as a **command name**, never executed — so uv never ran. The staged update silently installed nothing and the `mcc-*` commands were never created. The user saw \"Update staged for after restart\" with no error, then `mcc-claude` was \"not recognized\".\n\n## The fix\n\nThe helper now emits the uv path and the argument array as real PowerShell values and calls uv through the call operator:\n\n```powershell\n$uvPath = '<...>'\n$installArgs = @('tool','install','--force',...)\n& $uvPath @$installArgs 2>&1 | Out-String | Out-Null\n```\n\nSo once the launchers exit, the detached helper actually runs `uv tool install --force ... my-claude-code @ file:///...` and the `mcc-*` command family is created — the same outcome as the WSL/Linux direct path.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced the PowerShell bug: a string at statement position does not execute its inner command (the literal string was written, the command never ran).\n- Ran the real `Start-DeferredInstall` against a stub `uv` with a live process: the detached helper invoked `uv tool install --force ... my-claude-code @ file:///...` after the process exited.\n- Added an end-to-end regression test (`test_install_ps1_deferred_helper_runs_uv`) that loads the real function, points it at a stub uv, and asserts uv is invoked; plus a static guard asserting the helper uses `& $uvPath @$installArgs`. Both pass.\n- Full installer test file: 3 new tests pass; the 6 pre-existing PS harness failures are identical on this branch and on unmodified `fork/main` (a checksum-fixture issue, out of scope).\n\nVersion 5.2.1 -> 5.2.2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
