    "message": "fix(install): deferred Windows update now actually runs uv and creates the mcc-* commands\n\nThe deferred (app-running) install path staged a verified wheel and spawned a\ndetached helper, but the helper invoked uv by placing a command STRING at\nstatement position (`$argumentsLiteral 2>&1 | Out-String`). In PowerShell a\nstatement-position string is treated as a command NAME, never executed, so uv\nnever ran: the staged update installed nothing and the mcc-* commands were never\ncreated -- the user saw \"staged for after restart\" with no error and then\n`mcc-claude` not recognized.\n\nThe helper now emits `$uvPath` and `$installArgs` as real PowerShell values and\ncalls `& $uvPath @$installArgs`, so the detached helper actually runs\n`uv tool install` once the launchers exit, matching the WSL/Linux outcome.\n\nAdds an end-to-end regression test that loads the real Start-DeferredInstall,\npoints it at a stub uv, and asserts uv is invoked (previously this path was\nuntested). Static guard asserts the helper invokes uv via the call operator.\n\nVerified: ran Start-DeferredInstall against a stub uv with a live process; the\ndetached helper invoked `uv tool install --force ... my-claude-code @ file:///...`.\n3 new deferred tests pass; the 6 pre-existing PS harness failures are unchanged\non both the branch and unmodified fork/main (a checksum-fixture issue, out of scope).\n\nVersion 5.2.1 -> 5.2.2 (installer deferred-install fix).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
